{%- comment -%}
  The custom properties a block's spacing settings resolve to, for the `style`
  attribute of any theme block that offers them.

      style="{% render 'block-spacing', margin: block.settings.margin, padding: block.settings.padding %}"

  Accepts `margin`, `padding` and `gap`, each a step name — tiny, small, medium,
  large, xlarge — and prints only the ones it was given. An unrecognised value
  prints nothing rather than `var(--step-)`, which would be an invalid property
  and take the whole declaration with it.

  **The stylesheet decides what each property does; this only says how much.**
  A block writes `--block-margin` and its own class chooses whether that is a
  gap below, a gap either side, or a ratio of the two — which is why the eyebrow
  can keep its tight-above proportion while sharing one merchant-facing scale
  with everything else. It is also why the fallback lives in the CSS: a block
  whose setting is untouched writes nothing at all, and the class keeps whatever
  spacing it had before the control existed.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  **`none` had to be handled, not skipped.** It is an offered value for padding
  and gap, and it fell outside the step list — so choosing None printed nothing
  at all, the class kept its own fallback, and the control did nothing. That
  reads as a broken setting rather than an empty one, which is exactly what it
  was reported as.

  It prints `0` rather than `var(--step-none)`: whether that token exists is a
  question the caller should not have to ask, and a `var()` that resolves to
  nothing takes the whole declaration with it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign steps = 'tiny,small,medium,large,xlarge' | split: ','
-%}
{%- if margin == 'none' %}--block-margin: 0;{% elsif steps contains margin %}--block-margin: var(--step-{{ margin }});{% endif -%}
{%- if padding == 'none' %}--block-padding: 0;{% elsif steps contains padding %}--block-padding: var(--step-{{ padding }});{% endif -%}
{%- if gap == 'none' %}--block-gap: 0;{% elsif steps contains gap %}--block-gap: var(--step-{{ gap }});{% endif -%}
